# armour/woman/padded: the padded gambeson cut to the woman (LADDER-ARMOUR, STYLE_P2 25.2 / 25.3 / 27.2): the man's quilted
# coat with her waist a pixel narrower; the stuffed rows bulge past the step-1 quilt seams (the first seam is her one
# shading row across the chest); a high collar with a clasp, a plain belt, a stuffed skirt flaring a pixel at the hem.
# Lit plane top-left (step 3, one step-4 shine on the lit shoulder), turn step 2, shadow step 1.
# Finish regions: R the collar's rim and the hem, P the lit chest, G the clasp, N the quilt seams, W the patch.
# Keys: rest idle run runl drawn swing lie in D U R L. Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h. Source: LADDER-ARMOUR's expand.py.
# (LADDER-ARMOUR i3) the quilt softened: the lit side's seam rows a step up (8/7, not 8/6), so the T1 coat reads as stuffed
# cloth and not as bandage stripes; the shadow side keeps its flat step 1.
# (FORGE-TORSO round 2 i2) the quilt channels' N marks dropped (no finish rides them; the T1 coat stays plain at 1x).
use person
body woman
role armour padded
layer torso
anchor neck
keys torso
z 2
# (ladder i2, integration) her quilt in undyed linen (her tunic's apron is cloth3 buff, the man's gambeson colour): the T1
# coat reads as a coat over her tunic
# (LADDER-ARMOUR polish i1, P3) quilting in vertical 3 px channels (a seam one step under its channel); the
# silhouette (bust, waist) as drawn: the old horizontal bands read as bandages.
legend 5 linen 0
legend 6 linen 1
legend 7 linen 2
legend 8 linen 3
legend 9 linen 4

